**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
# Every .env at any depth: a stray packages/database/.env inside an image would silently
# override the container's DATABASE_URL with a localhost value.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
docs
test-results
playwright-report
*.log

# TLS material and the ACME webroot.
#
# certbot writes these as root into the working tree, so from the first certificate onward
# `docker compose build` died on "permission denied" reading the build context - a break that
# only ever appears on a host that has actually gone live. And had it succeeded it would have
# been worse: every private key copied into every image layer.
infrastructure/nginx/certs
infrastructure/nginx/acme
